[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=User Guide
GenericName=Your first week with Dagric
Comment=The short read: updates, printers, Wi-Fi, shortcuts, and making the desktop yours
# guide/, not welcome/. Everything above describes the user guide — updates,
# printers, Wi-Fi, shortcuts, making the desktop yours are five of its headings
# and one of the welcome page's — but this line opened the welcome page, so the
# guide had no launcher entry at all and was reachable only from the setup
# wizard's last screen, once. The welcome page keeps `dagric-welcome`.
#
# AND THE NAME WAS THE HALF THAT STAYED WRONG. Exec, GenericName and Comment
# were all corrected to the user guide; `Name=` was left reading "Welcome
# Guide", which is what the Hub calls a DIFFERENT document — the Hub's "Welcome
# page — what Dagric promises" row runs dagric-welcome — so an owner who read
# the Hub and then went looking in the launcher for the welcome page clicked
# "Welcome Guide" and got the user guide. It now reads "User Guide": the same
# words the setup wizard's last screen shows on its card and the same words the
# document's own title uses. The five Name[xx] below are the existing
# msgid "User Guide" translations from po/*.po, not new wording, so the launcher
# entry and the wizard card cannot say two different things in German.
#
# And it is dagric-guide, not a bare firefox call, because Exec is a FIXED
# string: the guide now also ships as guide/de/index.html, and a German menu
# entry that opens English text reads as a broken translation. The wrapper
# resolves de_AT -> de -> English at launch.
Exec=dagric-guide
Icon=dagric-guide
Terminal=false
Categories=System;Documentation;
Keywords=welcome;guide;help;getting started;first week;start here;tour;intro;docs;faq;

# Localised keys below are generated by tools/i18n-desktop.py.
# Machine translation, unreviewed -- see the header of po/de.po.
# Edit the table in that script, not these lines.
